<title>USA: US exporters report soybeans sold to S. Korea-USDA.</title>
<headline>US exporters report soybeans sold to S. Korea-USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Monday said private exporters reported sales of 120,000 tonnes of soybeans to South Korea for delivery during the 1997/98 marketing year.</p>
<p>The marketing year for soybeans began Sept. 1.</p>
<p>Exporters must report to USDA sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of one commodity made in one day to a single destination by 1500 ET the next business day after the sale.</p>
<p>Sales of lesser quantities must be reported weekly.</p>
<p>((-- Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8394))</p>
